      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u give me a quick summary of the steps a company needs to follow when someone submits a \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR? i need to make sure we have the process right for our internal memo.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. **Receive and Verify Request**: Receive the “right to be forgotten” request and verify the identity of the data subject.\n2. **Assess Applicability**: Check if the request is valid under GDPR by determining whether the data is capable of being erased.\n3. **Evaluate Exemptions**: Assess whether there are any legitimate grounds for retaining the data (e.g., legal claims, public interest, etc.).\n4. **Identify and Remove Data**: Locate and erase the personal data wherever it is stored and ensure that all copies are removed.\n5. **Notify Relevant Parties**: Inform any third parties that were involved in handling the data about the erasure.\n6. **Comply with Records Retention**: Update the organization's records to reflect the erasure and maintain logs of the process.\n7. **Confirm Compliance**: Send a final confirmation to the data subject that their request has been processed, or explain the reasons if it has not.\n\nNote: Review any obligations to inform other entities about the erasure process if applicable.",
